  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Chef Viktor is angry because Senya and Fedya got fired. He reassigns their names to the remaining cooks in the kitchen. Let's listen closely to their exchange in Russian first, and then walk through each line together.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "viktor",
      "t": "Сеня, соус готов?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "artyom",
      "t": "А я не Сеня.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "artyom",
      "t": "Я Артем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "viktor",
      "t": "Сеню уволили.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "viktor",
      "t": "Мне плевать, кто ты.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "viktor",
      "t": "Сегодня ты Сеня.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "viktor",
      "t": "Федя бы это быстро сделал.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я тоже Федя, шеф.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "viktor",
      "t": "Нет, ты не Федя.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "viktor",
      "t": "Имя Федя заслужить надо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "viktor",
      "t": "Теперь ты Артем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, шеф.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Let's walk through it together.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "viktor",
      "t": "Сеня, соус готов?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Senya, is the sauce ready?' — Notice the proper name meaning 'Senya' paired with the noun for 'sauce'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "artyom",
      "t": "А я не Сеня.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am not Senya.' Notice the word order: 'I' comes first, and 'Senya' finishes the sentence.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "artyom",
      "t": "Я Артем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am Artyom.' Here 'I' sets up the idea, while 'Artyom' comes at the end for emphasis. Viktor answers straight away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "viktor",
      "t": "Сеню уволили.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Senya got fired.' — Notice the proper name meaning 'Senya' paired with the verb for 'to fire, to dismiss'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "viktor",
      "t": "Мне плевать, кто ты.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I do not care who you are.' The first content word means 'to me', and 'you' rounds out the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "viktor",
      "t": "Сегодня ты Сеня.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Today you are Senya.' A compact expression built around 'today' and 'Senya'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "viktor",
      "t": "Федя бы это быстро сделал.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Fedya would have done it fast.' — Notice the proper name meaning 'Fedya' paired with the pronoun for 'this'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я тоже Федя, шеф.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am Fedya too, Chef.' In Russian, 'I' leads into 'chef' in a very natural everyday phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "viktor",
      "t": "Нет, ты не Федя.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'No, you are not Fedya.' In Russian, 'you' leads into 'Fedya' in a very natural everyday phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "viktor",
      "t": "Имя Федя заслужить надо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You have to earn the name Fedya.' The key word here means 'name', which Viktor combines with 'Fedya'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "viktor",
      "t": "Теперь ты Артем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Now you are Artyom.' Notice the word order: 'now' comes first, and 'Artyom' finishes the sentence.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, шеф.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, Chef.' — Built around the key proper name meaning 'chef, boss'. Now listen to the whole scene again.",
